    "narrative": "Today\u2019s outlook for Ghost Ride the WHIP hinges on capitalizing on high-ceiling matchups in the outfield, with **James Wood** (76.27) and **Brice Turang** (75.05) anchoring the offense as our clear daily leaders. **James Wood** is in a prime spot against Kelly with a favorable 4.74 xERA and an elite 0.401 xwOBA, while **Brice Turang** benefits from a slow-delivering pitcher that bolsters his stolen base profile\u2014a critical factor given our league's scarcity-weighted scoring. **Seiya Suzuki** also draws a strong 72.03 projection, buoyed by favorable wind conditions blowing out at his home park. While **Corbin Carroll** is facing a tougher lefty in Griffin (3.81 xERA) and suffers from a platoon dip, his floor remains high enough to warrant a start in the OF5 slot over more volatile options.\n\nEfficiency remains the name of the game, which is why **Zach McKinstry** finds himself on the pine with a 38.67 score, falling just short of our 40-point \"Zebras\" floor. Despite the favorable park factors against Woo, the combined negative impact of an #8 batting order placement and the pitcher's quality led the optimizer to prioritize the more productive spots held by **Travis Bazzana** (59.97) and **Josh Naylor** (61.00). We are monitoring the 38% rain risk surrounding **Vinnie Pasquantino**; while his 59.39 score suggests a solid start, any weather-induced delay could hamper his rhythm against Matthews. With **Trevor Story** and **Mickey Moniak** still on the shelf, we continue to rely on the depth of our bench including **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Max Muncy**, and **Gabriel Moreno** to rotate in as injury and rest management require throughout the week, alongside prospects like **Carson Williams** and **Dalton Rushing** waiting in the wings.",
